{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed from Raamses in the first month on the fifteenth day</b> etc. In Egypt they were not commanded regarding Yom Tov — only regarding leaven, the first night." "<b>On the morrow of the Passover.</b> The day of the fifteenth — and the first night is called Passover, because they are occupied with the sacrifice that is called by that name. A proof for this is from the portion of Emor and from the portion of Pinchas. But the rest of the festival, from the first night onward, is called חג המצות, the Festival of Matzot."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {1 "The parenthetical (ט״ו) appears to be a variant reading or marginal notation for טוב; translated according to context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:33.088133122Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}